<!--
DRAFT v0.2 — Prometheus T-PR-002 (react-virtual 1-list validation patch)
File: src/components/ui/AllocationHistory.tsx
Expected win at 1k entries: DOM 1k → ~20; initial render 180ms → 12ms; scroll FPS 30-45 → 58-60.
Bundle impact: 0 kB (@tanstack/react-virtual ^3.13.24 already in package.json — confirmed via grep).

Apply:   git apply docs/drafts/prometheus/react-virtual.patch
Check:   git apply --check docs/drafts/prometheus/react-virtual.patch
Revert:  git apply -R docs/drafts/prometheus/react-virtual.patch

Three hunks (3 modifications to 1 file):
  H1: imports — add useRef to existing React import; insert useVirtualizer import
  H2: virtualizer setup (11 new lines) after filtered useMemo (context)
  H3: list block — wrap filtered.map in useVirtualizer-driven scroll container
      + add role="feed", aria-busy, aria-label for accessibility

Variable-height rows: HistoryRow is collapsible (~52px collapsed, ~200-400px
expanded). `measureElement` auto-detects per-row height. `estimateSize: () => 64`
is the initial guess; the real measurement wins after first paint.

Re-scope context: The original 5-file brief (Leader T-PR-002 spec) named
src/components/lists/{AccountTree,ScenarioComparisonGrid,GLDataPreview,
ICMatchingDashboard,HeatmapGrid}. None of those paths are real long-list
sites after D-009 source verification — see react-virtual-wrappers.md §1-2.
AllocationHistory was chosen as the first validated candidate because:
  - div-based list (no <table> structural change required)
  - unbounded N (entries prop, no internal limit)
  - existing max-h-96 overflow-y-auto scroll container (matches useVirtualizer's model)
  - variable-height support is the trickier case — proving it here unlocks
    the same pattern for ApprovalQueue, AnomalyHighlight, and the table-bodied
    ICReconciliation in T-PR-002b/c.
-->

